New task for you as the independent incident-independence reviewer: the independent check of the U2 corrected proposition. The brief is committed before issue (your condition C5) at `level4/closure_proofs/p5y_k5_cell309_p309_r1/reviews/BRIEF_U2_CHECK_P309.md` (commit 46533afd, pushed; branch HEAD 7273b76e). Read it first and follow its firewall exactly.

Context: your review is committed verbatim (39ed662c, sha f5ff1d68…). The owner has since ruled on U2 (verbatim in `governance/OWNER_RULINGS_2_P309_VERBATIM.md`, section "OWNER RULING — U2"). The ruling confirms NOT_TRIGGERED only on the corrected premise, established from committed evidence; otherwise the campaign STOPs with U2_UNRESOLVED. The owner said: "Do not reinterpret U2 merely to make the campaign proceed."

The document to check is `governance/U2_CORRECTED_PROPOSITION.md`. Its mechanical evidence is:
- `code/u2_structure_check.py` → `evidence/u2/U2_STRUCTURE_CHECK.json`;
- `tests/test_u2_structure_controls.py` → `evidence/u2/U2_CONTROLS.json`;
- `code/code_skeleton.py`, the firewalled reader you must use for the consumer files and the input-file structure.

Be adversarial. In particular, check whether:
- the S1 identities actually support "no new function of adopted scalars";
- §5 misses or mis-classifies any quantity;
- the Q1–Q5 criterion stretches the committed record.

Write `reviews/REVIEW_U2_CHECK_P309.md`, with line 2 exactly `U2_CP_ESTABLISHED` (plus any conditions) or `U2_UNRESOLVED` (plus the reasons). Make no git writes. Ledger every read and execution to a scratch file under /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ReBaseGuard/ea54e9f6-e828-5447-be15-220ef2c329fd/scratchpad/u2check/ and name it in your output. Report the verdict lines and a short summary when done.

Your earlier report was right on all four points, and the owner has now ruled on each. The rulings are verbatim in `level4/closure_proofs/p5y_k5_cell309_p309_r1/governance/OWNER_RULINGS_2_P309_VERBATIM.md`:
- the test band moves out of the real band;
- a narrow scanner allowance covers the marker name;
- a sandbox ref with the real marker name counts as marker creation and is FORBIDDEN (use the synthetic TEST_ONLY_DO_NOT_EXECUTE_P309_MARKER);
- you are explicitly authorized to write and test the admission mechanism, but not to issue a grant or lift the quarantine.

Your task is committed before issue in `reviews/BRIEF_FC2_VERIFIER_VARIANT_AUTHOR.md` (commit on branch HEAD 78bd6a98, pushed). The spec is `fc2/FC2_SPEC_R2.md`, which supersedes rev. 1. Read both in full and follow them exactly. In particular:
- the variant is `verify/srk_verify_indep_scoped.py`, not "_granted" (the push procedure refuses paths containing GRANT);
- the TEST band is the drift hull of the declared synthetic h3 decoy cell, and its committed certificates are the positive-path fixtures, so no producer run is needed;
- the REAL band is geometry-blind, and real-band tests are dry only;
- never create any ref under refs/p5y-k5-cell309-p309-r1/, anywhere;
- never write the production grant path;
- do not read producer or guard code.

Your four spec-ambiguity points from last time are resolved in rev. 2 §§2–4. Where rev. 2 leaves something open, resolve it conservatively (fail closed) and report how.

If the tooling denies a write again, stop and report it. Do not look for another way to get the write done.

When done, report:
- the variant and harness sha256;
- the diff summary;
- per-test results;
- the I1 summary and any differences;
- the ambiguities you resolved;
- the §9 independence statement.
